endar/credentials.json` or `NOTION_CALENDAR_AUTHORIZATION` / `NOTION_CALENDAR_TOKEN`. JWT lasts ~**5 hours** — on 401/403 ask to refresh the session secret; do not invent tokens.\n2. **Order**: `get_user` → pick `provider` + `accountId` → `get_calendar_lists` → then events.\n3. **Voice**: **title/summary first**, never lead with ids. JSON tool results may include ids — when speaking to the user, lead with the human label.\n4. **create_event**: `eventData` needs `id` (uuid hex ok), `summary`, `start`, `end`, `status`, `provider`, `accountId`, `calendarId`, `reminders:{useDefault:true}`. Use `start`/`end` only (no `startTime`/`endTime`). Default `send_updates` to `none` unless the user wants guest emails.","confidence":0.7,"evidence":{},"finding":"credentials.json","finding_ids":["finding-d604dcefb17e4e42a435ce47b38f527e"],"id":"sha256:b5eab827c08d8378f8c261c864f150ca0da91e9ad3d730731812c3382ded4d40","intent":null,"line":32,"match_fingerprint":"07a0b37ad28a14919446682ad9b1f38223a950eb02c424e48b49fe75c25268c0","message":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-d604dcefb17e4e42a435ce47b38f527e","line":32,"path":"SKILL.md","start_column":40}],"path":"SKILL.md","pattern":"Credential Access","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"PE3","severity":"HIGH","start_column":40,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"]}],"findings_truncated":false,"freshness":"current","id":"plugin:community:3f746959c82ea2fc91a6f9be055d6772/notion-calendar","kind":"plugin_skill","plugin_path":"","profile":{"digest":"sha256:a73e7c4a9fa0ac563a885c541d207e90dde2e248ca426f7824cf429d725db921","id":"static-standard-v3"},"raw_finding_count":1,"report_digest":"sha256:9bfdd92c95a415